Changes to Klipper that Rebuild builds its MCU firmware with, while they are
waiting to be merged upstream. They are applied to the Klipper checkout only
for the firmware builds and reverted afterwards, so Klipper itself stays a
clean upstream checkout that Moonraker can update. They touch only MCU code
(src/), so the host side needs none of them.

  0001            ar100: Utilize serial_irq.c code for message parsing and
                  generation - Kevin's, from KevinOConnor/klipper-dev
                  work-ar100-20260928; he left it out when committing the rest
                  and asked for it to be submitted with the Kconfig changes
  0002            ar100: select SERIAL and default SERIAL_BAUD to 1500000;
                  without it the serial_irq.c code has a baud rate of 0 and
                  clock sync fails with NaN

